# Google Gemma 4 12B — findings by Nemotron 3.5 Super VL 120B A12B

> Source: Google DeepMind (gemma-4-12b-unified)
> Date: 2026-10-25 (UTC)
> Overview and scoring methodology: ../../model-comparison.md
> Cross-model signed log: ../../model-findings.md

## Model card

- **Name:** Gemma 4 12B
- **Short description:** Open-weight multimodal model from Google DeepMind; 12B parameters; handles text+image input (audio supported on 12B variant), text output; Apache 2.0 license.
- **Provider / access:** Hugging Face (google/gemma-4-12B variants), Google AI Studio, Gemini API, Kaggle, local run via Ollama/LM Studio/llama.cpp/MLX/LiteRT-LM.
- **Release / knowledge:** Gemma 4 released June 2026; model card last updated 2026-07-30. Knowledge cutoff not stated.
- **IDs:** `gemma-4-12b` (Google), `google/gemma-4-12b` / `google/gemma-4-12b-it` (HF).
- **Context window:** Up to 256K tokens (official model card); 262k/260k tokens (Artificial Analysis).
- **Modalities:** Text + image input (+ audio supported on E2B/E4B/12B variants per official card); text output. Reasoning model (per AA). Function calling, thinking mode supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-25):** Open weights (Apache 2.0, self-hosted); Artificial Analysis lists API pricing $0.10 in / $0.30 out per 1M via 1 provider.
- **Architecture:** 12B parameters; open weights; license Apache 2.0; multimodal VLM architecture per official card.

### Raw benchmarks found

- Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: **14** (estimated; #20/141 open-weights, median 8); speed 114.2 tok/s (#22/64); cost $0.10 in / $0.30 out per 1M; context 262k tokens; TTFT 2.24s.
- benchgap (22 measured / 85 estimated, data 2026-10-24): GPQA Diamond 78.8% measured; MMLU-Pro 77.2% measured; LiveCodeBench v6 72.0% measured; SWE-bench Verified 57.7% estimated ±6.4 pp; IFEval 93.2% estimated ±2.7 pp; MMLU 86.0% estimated ±1.8 pp; MMMU 78.8% estimated ±1.0 pp; MATH-500 95.2% estimated ±3.1 pp; HLE 15.4% estimated ±6.5 pp; AIME26 77.5% measured; MathVision 79.7% measured; MedXpertQA (MM) 48.7% measured.
- Conflicts: context window official 256K vs AA 262k/260k (minor); modalities official lists text+image (+audio on 12B) while AA lists text+image+speech+video; AA Intelligence Index is estimated (not measured).

### Normalized scores (1–100)

- Tool use: **72/100.** Function calling supported per official card; benchgap Toolathon 27.0% estimated; capped by limited independent agentic tool-use replication.
- Reasoning: **74/100.** AA Intelligence Index 14 (est) above class median; GPQA Diamond 78.8% measured; HLE only ~15% caps reasoning.
- Context window: **80/100.** 256K–262K tokens; strong for a 12B model.
- Multimodal: **85/100.** Native text+image input (+audio on 12B), text out; image benchmarks strong (MMMU 78.8% est, AI2D_TEST 90.1% est).
- Coding: **72/100.** LiveCodeBench v6 72.0% measured; SWE-bench Verified 57.7% estimated; solid but not frontier-leading.
- Cost efficiency: **80/100.** Apache 2.0 open weights; API pricing $0.10/$0.30 per 1M is near class medians ($0.12/$0.30).
- **Overall Score: 78/100.** Half-up mean of the five non-cost dims; best-fit recommendation: compact multimodal reasoning model for on-device and edge deployment where Apache 2.0 openness and 12B scale matter.

